On Mon, 1 Aug 2011, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Haven't checked the sources; my guess would be that the original
> counter may stay untouched when the guaranteed appearance gets
> triggered?

Yes, it's untouched.

The relevant variable is "u.udg_cnt".  The only times it is changed:

 * (allmain.c) reduce by 1 on each turn when not zero, not counting
   invulnerable turns due to prayer.
 * (allmain.c) when zero, do an "intervene" and set to 50--249
 * (spell.c) on successful invocation, set to 2D6, unless
   that would increase it.
 * (u_init.c) set to zero at start of game.
 * (wizard.c) set to 50--299 at the wizard's first death, unless
   the invocation was performed earlier.

So you could get three Rodneys in a 50-move period...

